ARRAY PROBLEM-SOLVING — LEVEL 1(manam Turn a problem statement into a sequence of operations)
#Problem 1 — Find the Maximum
arr = [12, 45, 7, 89, 23, 56] #89
"max(arr)"  -> That uses Python's built-in and skips the actual problem-solving

##First pseudocode raaskondi ilaa:
max_value = first element
12 -> max = 12
45 -> 45 > 12 → max = 45
7  -> 7 > 45  → no
89 -> 89 > 45 → max = 89
23 -> 23 > 89 → no
56 -> 56 > 89 → no
answer = 89

arr = [12, 45, 7, 89, 23, 56]
max_value = arr[0]
for i in arr:
    if i > max_value:
        max_value = i
print(max_value) #O(n) time kadaa

